@startuml
title Room Access and Monitored 1:1 Chat Policy
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center
skinparam activity {
  BackgroundColor #F8FAFC
  BorderColor #334155
  DiamondBackgroundColor #FFF7D6
  DiamondBorderColor #A16207
}

start
:Policy Sync reads Keycloak users, effective Matrix entitlement,\nclearance, room roles and direct group memberships;
:Require current Matrix entitlement and a recognized clearance;
if (Configured managed room?) then (yes)
  :Require clearance rank >= room minimum;
  :Require exactly one explicit room role;
  :Join OrgBot at PL 0 and check its authenticated readiness;
  :Set membership and Matrix power level;
  note right
    Clearance: basis < intern < vertraulich < streng_vertraulich.
    Role power: reader 0, writer 10, moderator 50.
    Rooms are invite-only, joined-history and Megolm encrypted.
    Clearance labels do not change E2EE strength.
  end note
else (direct chat)
  :Require both users share the same exact group ID;
  :Require group name prefix `1to1chat.`;
  :Create private non-federated room with signed pair marker;
  :Invite OrgBot and peer; require Megolm and joined Bot;
endif
:Synapse rechecks current policy and room state on each action;
if (Current authorization and required room state valid?) then (yes)
  :Allow only the actions granted by room power / pair policy;
else (no)
  :Deny new access or actions;
endif
stop

note right
  Ordinary organization/department groups grant no 1:1 access.
  Nested-group inheritance and the `m.direct` client hint are
  not authorization. Missing or expired policy fails closed;
  revocation removes known unauthorized room memberships.
  Bot readiness/membership does not prove every decryption key.

  The MAS-specific Keycloak flow requires `matrix-access`.
  Current policy snapshots carry that grant for room and
  export authorization.
  Verify the configured mappings and enforcement for each
  deployment.
end note
@enduml
